From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:08:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D309 tui: name models in a session whose location is
 unavailable

Upstream: the transcript names models from the session's location's model list. When that location is unavailable (its directory is gone), the list never loads and every assistant footer and model-switch notice shows the raw ID (`openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`) instead of the model's name.
Fixed: until the session's location has a model list, names come from the default location's list (raw IDs remain the fallback for models neither knows).
Scenarios: tui/session-history.test.ts "a session whose directory is gone"
Upstream tests: none changed

diff --git a/packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx b/packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx
index 33bd34340e..dafbc53cc1 100644
--- a/packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx
+++ b/packages/tui/src/routes/session/index.tsx
@@ -260,7 +260,8 @@ export function Session(props: {
     commands: [{ bind: "escape,ctrl+c", title: "Close sidebar", group: "Session", run: props.onToggleSidebar }],
   }))
   const contentWidth = createMemo(() => (props.width ?? dimensions().width - props.verticalTabsWidth) - 4)
-  const models = createMemo(() => data.location.model.list(location()) ?? [])
+  // A session whose location is unavailable never loads its models: name them from the default location's.
+  const models = createMemo(() => data.location.model.list(location()) ?? data.location.model.list() ?? [])
 
   const scrollAcceleration = createMemo(() => getScrollAcceleration(config))
   const toast = useToast()
